# The in-tree prover-endpoint round trip
# (docs/spec/endpoints.md §§6.3–6.4): a toy prover-skeleton run emits proof
# bytes the derived toy verifier endpoint accepts — derived orchestration on
# both sides, with both replica sponges deriving the same challenge stream. The
# negative cases hold the refusal/defect/verdict boundaries apart: a cheating supplier
# is refused by the verifier's checks (a verdict), a missing supplier is
# a profile refusal (E407), a boundary-violating fill is a defect
# (E408), a wrong endpoint kind is E409, missing inputs are E410.

# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: zkc-opt %pir-seal-full %S/../Encoding/routed-schnorr.mlir -o %t/sealed.mlir
# RUN: zkc-opt %pir-project-full %t/sealed.mlir -o %t/verifier.mlir
# RUN: zkc-opt %pir-project-prover-full %t/sealed.mlir -o %t/prover.mlir

# The round trip: witness x=5 (y = 4^5 = 1024), nonce k=7.
# RUN: zkc-run %t/prover.mlir --prove "w=00000000000000050000000000000007" --statement "y=1024" --verify-with %t/verifier.mlir | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: prove: emitted 16 bytes
# CHECK: prover challenges: 1405996128736189831
# CHECK: proof: 0000000000004000018f822624796d07
# CHECK: verifier verdict: accept
# CHECK: round trip: the derived prover's bytes are accepted by the derived verifier, and both replicas derived the same challenge stream

# The cheating supplier: boundary-conformant, wrong algebra, run under
# the honest derived orchestration — and rejected exactly where it must
# be, at the verifier's equation. Transcript consistency is automatic
# (the orchestration fed it the real challenge), so the reject class is
# check_failure, not a decode failure.
# RUN: not zkc-run %t/prover.mlir --profile toy-cheat --prove "w=00000000000000050000000000000007" --statement "y=1024" --verify-with %t/verifier.mlir | FileCheck --check-prefix=CHEAT %s
# CHEAT: prove: emitted 16 bytes
# CHEAT: verifier verdict: check_failure
# CHEAT: round trip: FAILED

# A hole contract with no supplier in the executing profile is a
# refusal naming the digest, never a verdict (E407). The digest is
# rewritten and the identity re-minted, so the refusal under test is
# the supplier gate's, not the identity gate's.
# RUN: sed 's/sha256:b939155d962c0e82baee8477daebdd8168d59a1c828dabfd8f5724ab18b13e15/sha256:9999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999/' %t/prover.mlir > %t/unsupplied-raw.mlir
# RUN: zkc-translate --oir-id %t/unsupplied-raw.mlir -o %t/unsupplied.id
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/rewrite-artifact-id.py oir.artifact %t/unsupplied-raw.mlir %t/unsupplied.mlir %t/unsupplied.id
# RUN: not zkc-run %t/unsupplied.mlir --prove "w=00000000000000050000000000000007" --statement "y=1024" 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=E407 %s
# E407: [zkc-E407] hole contract 'sha256:9999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999' (kind 'commit') has no supplier in profile 'toy'

# A fill that reports a defect at its own boundary is E408 — here the
# witness payload is eight bytes where the sigma convention needs
# sixteen, and the supplier says so.
# RUN: not zkc-run %t/prover.mlir --prove "w=0000000000000005" --statement "y=1024" 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=E408 %s
# E408: [zkc-E408] fill for hole contract 'sha256:b939155d962c0e82baee8477daebdd8168d59a1c828dabfd8f5724ab18b13e15' reported a defect

# The prove entry point executes prover skeletons only (E409).
# RUN: not zkc-run %t/verifier.mlir --prove "w=00000000000000050000000000000007" --statement "y=1024" 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=E409 %s
# E409: [zkc-E409] endpoint kind 'verifier' is not executable by the prove entry point

# A missing witness payload is an input refusal (E410).
# RUN: not zkc-run %t/prover.mlir --prove "unrelated=00" --statement "y=1024" 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=E410 %s
# E410: [zkc-E410] witness payload 'w' missing

# Twin parity for the prover leg: the reference twin runs the same
# derived document with its own toy fills and must reproduce the exact
# challenge stream and proof bytes the carrier emitted.
# RUN: zkc-run %t/prover.mlir --prove "w=00000000000000050000000000000007" --statement "y=1024" | grep -E "prover challenges|proof:" > %t/carrier.txt
# Only the twin's half needs uv, so only the twin's half is gated. A
# whole-file feature gate would take the four native refusals above with
# it, and on a machine without uv the suite would be green with them
# unexercised — which test/Lint/diagnostic-allocation.test now refuses.
# RUN: %if uv %{ %uv python -m oracle.exec derived-prove schnorr-routed "s:y=1024" "w:w=00000000000000050000000000000007" > %t/twin.txt %}
# RUN: %if uv %{ diff %t/carrier.txt %t/twin.txt %}
